<h3 id="design_and_display">Design and Display</h3><br/>
The Series 12 retains the same basic design introduced by the Series 10, including 42mm and 46mm size options and a 9.7mm-thick case. Nevertheless, Apple has made some subtle dimensional changes. Both sizes are now 1mm wider, and every equivalent aluminum or titanium configuration is between 2.1 and 3.3 grams heavier than its Series 10 counterpart.<br/>
<br/>
At the same time, the display has <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/10/apple-watch-series-12-has-smaller-screens/">shrunk slightly</a>. Resolution is unchanged, but the active display area is around 2% smaller on both sizes. The combination of a wider, receded case and smaller display produces thicker borders around the screen.<br/>
